---
const { money, income, esc, t, schedule, rows, cents, nlIncomeTax } =
  Astro.props;
---

<h2>Worked example at the median wage</h2>
<p>
  The same arithmetic the receipt runs, for{" "}
  <Fragment set:html={money(income)} /> of employment income in {t.year}. Redo
  it with a calculator, or check it against form NL428 (lines 27 and 29 are the
  CPP and EI credits).
</p>
<Fragment
  set:html={await schedule({
    compact: true,
    cols: [
      {
        label: "Step",
      },
      {
        label: "Amount",
        num: true,
      },
    ],
    rows: rows.map((r) => ({
      cells: [esc(r[0]), r[1]],
    })),
  })}
/>
<p class="small">
  Without the CPP and EI credits and the enhanced CPP deduction, the same income
  would show{" "}
  <Fragment
    set:html={cents(
      nlIncomeTax(income, {
        ...t,
        cpp: undefined,
        ei: undefined,
      }),
    )}
  />
  .
</p>
